# Tenor notes: a compact ninth/third question develops into a higher reply. Expression: laid-back starts, detached pickups, a breath each bar and one accented peak.
# Trumpet notes: Harmon-muted answers occupy the tenor's rests. Expression: quiet separated answers, no unrecorded falls, scoops or shakes.
# Piano notes: rootless shell voicings answer the horns without doubling their rhythm. Expression: soft attacks, held second chords, an empty final half-bar.
# Bass notes: deliberate root-third-fifth connections with a restrained dominant walk. Expression: longer downbeats, lighter connectors and space under the cadence.
# Drums: the right hand owns ride, left hand sidestick, foot a sparse kick. Expression: lighter offbeats; final cymbal rings without a fill over the horns.
